  "Separating the event, its explanation, and its relevance helps readers follow fast-moving financial information. The aim is to help people understand a development without telling them what financial decision to make.": "分别交代事件、原因以及与读者的关系，有助于理解快速变化的财经信息。设计希望帮助用户看懂变化，不替他们做财务决策。",
  "Personal relevance depends on context and timing.": "个人相关性，离不开背景与时机。",
  "The design used a personalized introduction and separate views for market context and company events to show their relevance to the reader. The broader direction also considered Discover memory, explicit curation, and query analysis as possible ways to select relevant content. Because financial events change quickly, each view needed to explain why a development mattered now and avoid repeating details from other views.": "设计通过个性化开场，以及分别呈现市场背景和公司事件的视图，说明这些信息与读者的关系。在更广泛的设计探索中，也考虑过用 Discover 记忆、主动筛选和查询分析来判断内容是否相关。财经事件变化很快，每个视图都需要说明事件为什么现在值得关注，同时避免重复其他视图的信息。",
  "Feed": "信息流",
  "Introduce the event and why it matters, using a clear hierarchy so readers can scan for the main point.": "用清晰的信息层级介绍事件及其意义，方便读者快速找到重点。",
  "Detail": "详情",
  "Expand on the event and its context, adding to what readers saw in the feed.": "进一步说明事件和背景，补充信息流中尚未展开的内容。",
  "Connected dashboard": "关联看板",
  "In the broader design direction, connect individual updates to the wider financial picture so each view adds context instead of repeating another.": "在更广泛的设计探索中，将单条动态与整体财经状况联系起来，让各个界面补充不同的背景信息，减少重复。",
  "I drew on the clarity, scan-friendly hierarchy, and restraint of Bloomberg-style financial reporting. I used those qualities as a reference for helping readers stay oriented and confident, without copying the format.": "我参考了 Bloomberg 式财经报道清晰、易扫读且克制的呈现方式，希望帮助读者抓住重点、更有把握地理解信息，并未直接照搬它的形式。",
  "Mobile views preserve the story": "移动端延续信息脉络",
  "Keep the same information logic at a smaller scale.": "在更小的屏幕上延续相同的信息逻辑。",
  "In the layout review, I compared two independent choices: grouping market and company updates together or separating them in the introduction, and combining stock updates in one card or giving each its own card. The four combinations show the trade-offs. One introductory group reads as a continuous update; two distinguish market context from company news. A combined card keeps companies together, while separate cards give each company a clear boundary so readers can scan one at a time.": "布局评审时，我比较了两个独立选项：开场部分将市场与公司动态合在一组还是分成两组，以及个股动态放在同一张卡片还是分别呈现。四种组合各有取舍：一组开场内容读起来更连贯，两组则能区分市场背景与公司新闻；合并卡片把多家公司放在一起，独立卡片则为每家公司划出边界，让读者逐张浏览。",
  "Intro grouping": "开场内容分组",
  "Four mobile card-layout variants": "四种移动端卡片布局方案",
  "One group or two": "一组或两组",
  "Stock cards": "个股卡片",
  "Combined or separate": "合并或分开",
  "One group": "一组内容",
