  "04 / Fit the platform system": "04 / 对齐平台设计系统",
  "05 / Hand off validated decisions": "05 / 交付已验证的决策",
  "Turn scattered requirements into something people can review.": "将分散的需求转化为各方可以评审的原型。",
  "The tax-exemption operations request was complex, with requirements spread across a PRD and business-process documents. I started with the Microsoft Ads Platform shell, which included the design system and common patterns, and brought the requirements and workflow into VibeCanvas.": "税务豁免运营的需求较为复杂，分散在 PRD 和业务流程文档中。我从已有设计系统和常用模式的 Microsoft Ads Platform 产品框架入手，将现有需求和流程整理到 VibeCanvas 中。",
  "With AI coding assistance, I turned those documents into an interactive first proposal. Separate prototype branches let me compare directions and retain earlier versions, giving finance stakeholders and developers a working proposal to review.": "我借助 AI 编程辅助，把这些材料做成可交互的初步方案。不同原型分支既方便比较设计方向，也保留了早期版本，供财务同事和开发人员实际查看、评审。",
  "The first proposal helped reveal what the workflow did not need.": "初步方案帮助厘清流程并不需要什么。",
  "The first version explored a dashboard, bulk updates, record history, and additional guidance. During review, finance stakeholders and developers agreed that a broader operations console was unnecessary. The task was to upload records, choose an update, validate the records, submit valid ones, and resolve failures.": "初版探索了仪表盘、批量更新、记录历史和额外指引。评审时，财务同事和开发人员确认，无需搭建更完整的运营控制台。核心任务是上传记录、选择更新类型、验证记录、提交有效记录，再处理未通过的记录。",
  "I narrowed the workflow to three stages: Prepare, Validate, and Results. Batch actions included marking records as exempt or taxable and recording certificate-review outcomes. I left out the unnecessary reporting and history views to keep the workflow focused on processing tax records and reviewing results.": "我将流程收敛为准备、验证和查看结果三个阶段。批量操作包括将记录设为免税或应税，以及记录证书审核结果。方案去掉了不需要的报表和历史页面，集中处理税务记录及其结果。",
  "Reconcile changes before carrying a decision forward.": "在推进方案前，先核对需求变化。",
  "Requirements kept changing after the first review. I used WorkIQ to compare the latest SharePoint PRD updates and comments with the earlier version, distinguishing confirmed changes from open questions.": "首次评审后，需求仍在变化。我用 WorkIQ 将 SharePoint 中最新的 PRD 更新和批注与早期版本对照，区分已确认的变化和尚待澄清的问题。",
  "I incorporated confirmed feedback into a new prototype branch and kept open questions visible for review. This gave the team an updated proposal without treating unresolved assumptions as requirements.": "我把已确认的反馈更新到新的原型分支，并列出尚未解决的问题，供团队评审。这样既能跟进最新需求，也不会把未确认的假设当作要求。",
  "Make the working prototype fit the system it would use.": "让可交互原型贴合实际要用的系统。",
  "Frontend review found that the first interface resembled the platform but did not use its Storybook components. I kept the reviewed workflow and rebuilt the prototype with the platform's components, design tokens, and established patterns.": "前端评审发现，初版只是外观接近平台界面，并未使用平台的 Storybook 组件。我保留已评审的流程，用平台现有组件、设计变量和交互模式重建原型。",
  "The rebuilt prototype gave developers the reviewed workflow in the components and tokens they would use. It served as a design handoff; the full backend and operations tool were not being presented as shipped.": "重建后的原型使用开发人员实际会用到的组件和设计变量来呈现已评审流程，便于参照实现。这里交付的是设计原型，不代表完整后端和运营工具已经上线。",
  "05 / Hand off validated decisions": "05 / 交付已验证的决策",
  "Carry the agreed workflow into engineering.": "将达成共识的流程交给工程团队。",
  "After finance stakeholders reviewed the focused workflow, I added the agreed logic to the PRD for engineering. The handoff included a finance-reviewed prototype built with the platform's design system and a clearer reference for implementation.": "财务同事完成精简流程的评审后，我把确认的逻辑写入 PRD，交给工程团队。交付内容包括经过财务评审、采用平台设计系统的原型，以及更清楚的实现参考。",
  "After handoff, I heard that the production frontend closely followed the prototype's Storybook components and tokens, helping limit implementation effort and repeated rework.": "交付后，我了解到生产前端基本沿用了原型的 Storybook 组件和设计变量，有助于控制实现投入、减少反复返工。",
  "The prototype gave the team something to discuss. Review helped us understand the work, narrow the scope, and use the system the team would build with.": "原型让团队有了具体的讨论对象，评审则帮助我们理解实际工作、缩小范围，并采用团队实际使用的设计系统。",
  "The interface changed while the workflow stayed stable. Finance partners could continue reviewing the agreed logic, and frontend partners could assess how it worked with their components.": "界面调整时，流程保持不变。财务同事可以继续评审已确认的逻辑，前端团队则能结合实际组件评估实现方式。",
  "Workflow schematic showing an exploratory tax-operations prototype, frontend feedback about unused Storybook components, and a rebuild using actual system components while preserving the validated flow.": "流程示意：税务运营探索原型经过前端评审，发现未使用 Storybook 组件，随后保留已验证流程，改用真实组件重建。",
  "Earlier work · ByteDance": "早期作品 · 字节跳动",
  "Earlier work · Tencent": "早期作品 · 腾讯",
